          %h2#idea Idea
          .float_right_image{:style => "margin: -40px 0px -20px 10px"}
            %figure{:style => "margin: 0 0 0 0"}
              %img{:src => "/nlab/files/VacuumPairCreation.jpg", :width => "200px"}/
              %figcaption{:style => "text-align: center"}
                from
                %a{:href => "#Hebenstreit14"} Hebenstreit 14
          %p
            What came to be called the
            %em Schwinger effect
            (
            %a{:href => "#Sauter31"}> Sauter 31
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#HeisenbergEuler36"} Heisenberg-Euler 36
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Schwinger51"} Schwinger 51
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#AffleckManton82"} Affleck-Manton 82
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#AffleckAlvarezManton82"} Affleck-Alvarez-Manton 82
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+effect"} non-perturbative effect
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+polarization"} vacuum polarization
            expected in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+electrodynamics"} quantum electrodynamics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electric+field"} electric field
            causes
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electron"} electron
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positron"} positron
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pairs"} pairs
            to appear out of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum"} vacuum
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+chromodynamics"} quantum chromodynamics
            would lead to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deconfinement"} deconfinement
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quarks"} quarks
            in a strong
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electric+field"} electric field
          %p
            While the effect is clearly predicted by established
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+%28physics%29"} theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
            yet, since the required electric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strengths"} field strengths
            are so large. But recent experiments get close to the required intensities (
            %a{:href => "#Dunne09"}> Dunne 09
            ).
          %h2#the_field_strengths The field strengths
          %p
            We consider
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
