            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scale"} scale
            beyond which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+polarization"} vacuum polarization
            due to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schwinger+effect"} Schwinger effect
            counteracts the ambient electric field and/or leads to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+decay"} vacuum decay
          %p
            As a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentz+group"} Lorentz
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invariant"} invariant
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:LorentzInvariantFieldStrenghts"} (2)
            this
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schwinger+limit"} Schwinger limit
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electric+field"} electric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
            is:
          #eq:CriticalFieldStrengthLorentzInvariant.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (6)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mi crit
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi m
                        %mn 2
                      %msup
                        %mi c
                        %mn 3
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mi ℏ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{E}_{crit}
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\frac{
                  m^2 c^3
                  }{
                  e \hbar
                  }
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Dunne04"}> Dunne 04, (1.3)
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Martin07"} Martin 07, (40)
          %p Here
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charge"} charge
                of the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charged+particles"} charged particles
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
                of the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charged+particles"} charged particles
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
                is the
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/speed+of+light"} speed of light
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℏ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hbar
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Planck%27s+constant"} Planck's constant
          %p
            This is such that the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lorentz+force"} Lorentz force
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi crit
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi e
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mi crit
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F_{crit}
                  \\; \coloneqq \;
                  e
                  \\,
                  \\mathcal{E}_{crit}
          %p
            acting over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Compton+wavelength"} Compton wavelength
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi λ
                    %mi Comp
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mfrac
                    %mi ℏ
                    %mrow
                      %mi m
                      %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_{Comp} \;\coloneqq\; \frac{\hbar }{m c}
            equals the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rest+energy"} rest energy
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi m
                  %msup
                    %mi c
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} m c^2
            of the given
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charged+particle"} charged particle
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi F
                            %mi crit
                          %msub
                            %mi λ
                            %mi Comp
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo =
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi m
                          %msup
                            %mi c
                            %mn 2
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇔
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi ℰ
                            %mi crit
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mo =
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mfrac
                            %mrow
                              %mi m
                              %msup
                                %mi c
                                %mn 2
                            %mrow
                              %mi e
                              %msub
                                %mi λ
                                %mi Comp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  \&amp;
                  F_{crit} \lambda_{Comp}
                  \\; = \;
                  m c^2
                  \\\
                  \\Leftrightarrow
                  \\;\;\;
                  \&amp;
                  \\mathcal{E}_{crit}
                  \\; = \;
                  \\frac{
                  m c^2
                  }{
                  e \lambda_{Comp}
                  }
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p
            Expressing
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:CriticalFieldStrengthLorentzInvariant"} (6)
            in terms of the corresponding critical value
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi crit
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E_{crit}
            of the actual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electric+field"} electric
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
            %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ActualFieldStrengths"} (1)
            in the given Lorentz frame yields (
            %a{:href => "#HashimotoOkaSonoda14b"}> Hashimoto-Oka-Sonoda 14b, (2.17)
            ,
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "https://www.wolframalpha.com/input/?i=solve+for+e+%3A+c++%3D+Sqrt%5B+Sqrt%5B+%281%2F4%29*%28+e%5E2+-+b%5E2+%29%5E2+%2B+%28p%5E2%29*%28e%5E2%29+%5D+%2B+%281%2F2%29*+%28e%5E2+-+b%5E2%29++%5D+"} check
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi crit
                  %mo ,
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mi crit
                  %mphantom
                    %mi AA
                  %mo ⇔
                  %mphantom
                    %mi AA
                  %msub
                    %mi E
                    %mi crit
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %msub
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mi crit
                  %msqrt
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi ℰ
                          %mi crit
                          %mn 2
                        %mo +
                        %msup
                          %mi B
                          %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi ℰ
                          %mi crit
                          %mn 2
                        %mo +
                        %msubsup
                          %mi B
                          %mo ∥
                          %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathcal{E}(E_{crit}, B)
                  \\;=\;
                  \\mathcal{E}_{crit}
                  \\phantom{AA}
                  \\Leftrightarrow
                  \\phantom{AA}
                  E_{crit}
                  \\;=\;
                  \\mathcal{E}_{crit}
                  \\sqrt{
                  \\frac{
                  \\mathcal{E}_{crit}^2 + B^2
                  }
                  {
                  \\mathcal{E}_{crit}^2 + B_{\parallel}^2
                  }
                  }
          %p
            This happens to coincide with the critical field strength of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/DBI-action"} DBI-action
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "DBI-action#CriticalFieldStrength"} there
          %h3#InHolographicQCD In holographic QCD
          %p
            It has been argued that in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+models"} intersecting D-brane models
            the Schwinger effect is what is reflected by the non-linearities in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/DBI-action"} DBI-action
            on probe branes in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FCFT"} AdS/CFT
            (
            %a{:href => "#SemenoffZarembo11"}> Semenoff-Zarembo 11
            ) and on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavor+branes"} flavor branes
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"} holographic QCD
            (
            %a{:href => "#HashimotoOka13"}> Hashimoto-Oka 13
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#HashimotoOkaSonoda14a"} Hashimoto-Oka-Sonoda 14a
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#HashimotoOkaSonoda14b"} Hashimoto-Oka-Sonoda 14b
            = succeed "." do
              %em holographic Schwinger effect
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
